From: wasi-python-layer
Date: 2026-08-10
Subject: [PATCH] drop dtime_/etime_ (f2c timing intrinsics) — WASI has no process clocks

dtime_.c / etime_.c call times() (sys/times.h). wasi-libc hard-errors
without -D_WASI_EMULATED_PROCESS_CLOCKS, whose wall-clock semantics differ
from process CPU time. DTIME/ETIME are Fortran timing intrinsics — scipy
never references them (CPython's time module handles timing). Dropped per
plan Stage 11 failure class A; re-add with the emulation flag only if a
consumer ever needs them.
---
--- a/F2CLIBS/libf2c/Makefile
+++ b/F2CLIBS/libf2c/Makefile
@@ -51,7 +51,7 @@
 	open.o rdfmt.o rewind.o rsfe.o rsli.o rsne.o sfe.o sue.o\
 	typesize.o uio.o util.o wref.o wrtfmt.o wsfe.o wsle.o wsne.o xwsne.o
 QINT =	pow_qq.o qbitbits.o qbitshft.o ftell64_.o
-TIME =	dtime_.o etime_.o
+TIME =	# dtime_.o etime_.o dropped: use times() (WASI has no process clocks; see 0009)
 
 # If you get an error compiling dtime_.c or etime_.c, try adding
 # -DUSE_CLOCK to the CFLAGS assignment above; if that does not work,
